## How Instagram search works (follow this)
- Prefer **Accounts/People** queries: multi-word role + niche phrases that appear in display names and bios (e.g. "fitness coach", "branding agency").
- Instagram ranks accounts by text match on **name field, username, bio** — not by post grids.
- Niche phrases beat single generic words (`agency`, `web`, `design`) which return chrome/spam.
- Hashtags are weak for lead harvesting in 2025–2026; use them sparingly and only when niche (`#brandingagency`, not `#agency`).
- Avoid "X website" / "need a website" intent phrases — they rarely match business account names.
- Prefer identity labels businesses actually put in their name/bio.

